Revision history for Tira

0.15  2026-08-06
    - Added self-contained `-o table` HTML to combined and type-specific
      dashboard commands.
    - Added polished responsive Kanban styling, offline card selection, and
      interactive last-modified/reference sorting.
    - Preserved ref-only zero-JSON reads unless `--title` is requested.
    - Added three type-specific dashboard entrypoints and Playwright coverage.

0.14  2026-08-06
    - Made default dashboard output ref-only without opening record JSON.
    - Added `--title` for title-enriched summary output with one read per card.
    - Ordered every dashboard mode newest-first by file modification time with
      deterministic reference tie-breaking.
    - Retained complete record payloads for `-o json`.

0.13  2026-08-06
    - Accepted Developer Dashboard path aliases wherever a project directory
      selector is accepted, while retaining direct-path precedence.
    - Reused DD's registry/config model without shell execution and prevented
      alias targets from appearing in command results or selector errors.

0.12  2026-08-06
    - Reduced dashboard reads from one full-board scan per visible column to
      one scan per selected board.
    - Preserved byte-identical JSON structure, record order, column order, and
      Discard filtering while grouping records in memory.

0.11  2026-08-06
    - Made hierarchy nodes retain the complete record returned by direct show.
    - Added an explicit Children section to human hierarchy output.
    - Prevented sparse hierarchy nodes from producing warnings and false empty
      descriptions, assignments, priorities, or timestamps.

0.10  2026-08-06
    - Made search and replace `--field` repeatable and cumulative while
      preserving caller-supplied field order.
    - Standardized all search results as `{hits, count}`.
    - Strengthened checklist permanence documentation and added a concrete
      per-field import dry-run diff example.

0.09  2026-08-06
    - Added one-call full project export and explicit full record listing.
    - Added field-aware search and previewable project-wide text replacement.
    - Added dry-run, transactional ref-keyed JSON bulk import.
    - Added stable gate/evidence entry IDs and append-only correction
      annotations without general log mutation.
    - Added symmetric long-form aliases for acceptance and problem fields.

0.08  2026-08-05
    - Made attachment-add responses return the filename actually retained by
      the target attachment list.
    - Added `supplied_filename` and `deduped` response metadata so callers can
      detect filename collapse without rereading the record.
    - Proved independent record/comment deduplication, cross-record filename
      retention, and truthful remove/re-add behavior.

0.07  2026-08-05
    - Fixed silent data loss when updating key details, deliverables,
      acceptance criteria, test steps, BDD, or ATDD arrays.
    - Made included and excluded scope updates append consistently.
    - Preserved explicit `--set-*` wholesale replacement and repeated-argument
      ordering across SOWs, epics, and tickets.

0.06  2026-08-05
    - Added ordered checklists to SOWs, epics, and tickets.
    - Added checklist list, add, and update commands with immutable entry IDs,
      item/status values, timestamps, validation, and Markdown rendering.
    - Expanded the Docker suite while retaining 100% statement and subroutine
      coverage.

0.05  2026-08-05
    - Documented why Tira mirrors Jira's work model while using direct local
      files to reduce agent payload and request overhead.
    - Made CLI argv, comment files, YAML, JSON, and structured output explicitly
      UTF-8 while preserving raw attachment bytes.
    - Fixed long comments containing `£` and eliminated wide-character output
      warnings.
    - Added lossless isolated-byte recovery for records corrupted by the former
      mixed byte/character writer; the next mutation persists valid UTF-8.
    - Expanded the Docker suite to 404 assertions while retaining 100%
      statement and subroutine coverage.

0.04  2026-08-05
    - Removed attachment path output so managed storage locations are never
      returned by the CLI or engine.
    - Made attachment retrieval reject unsupported output formats before
      emitting content while preserving raw bytes and deleted markers.
    - Added path-secrecy acceptance coverage; the Docker suite now contains
      394 assertions with 100% statement and subroutine coverage.

0.03  2026-08-05
    - Added symmetric SOW, epic, and ticket planning metadata: singular
      assignee, reporter, labels, dates, SDLC gate, lifecycle, priority,
      fix version, affected versions, and generated immediate parent.
    - Added project-person activation and deactivation while retaining
      historical names and rejecting new ownership by inactive people.
    - Updated assignment commands to enforce one assignee per record.
    - Expanded the Docker suite to 10 files and 389 assertions while retaining
      100% statement and subroutine coverage.

0.02  2026-08-05
    - Implemented all 100 documented use cases across 70 CLI entrypoints.
    - Added project people and link types, board/column lifecycle and sync,
      complete record fields and movement, hierarchy, subitems, reciprocal
      links, assignments, comments, attachments, evidence, gates, search, and
      ordered Kanban dashboard output.
    - Added transactional rollback for reciprocal record writes and column
      filesystem/configuration changes.
    - Made project location intentionally opaque in the agent contract and CLI
      help so agents use commands instead of managed-storage edits.
    - Added full command-matrix, idempotency, rollback, and security tests while
      maintaining 100% statement and subroutine coverage.

0.01  2026-08-05
    - Established the governed filesystem-native Tira foundation.
    - Added project discovery and canonical `.tira` project creation.
    - Added independent SOW, epic, and ticket boards with protected Backlog and
      Discard columns and immutable increasing references.
    - Added free-ranging SOW, epic, and ticket creation with canonical JSON.
    - Added private project-context selection.
    - Added TOON-first, pretty JSON, and Markdown output modes.
    - Added the raw `dashboard tira.skills` agent manual command.
    - Expanded the agent manual with the complete technical command catalogue,
      argument rules, lifecycle semantics, and 100 numbered use cases.
    - Added atomic writes, project locking, counter validation, taint-safe path
      validation, Docker verification, and 100% coverage.
